      "id": "ch-002",
      "name": "Chapter 2 – Salt and Stone",
      "text": "{\\rtf1\\fbidis\\ansi\\ansicpg1252\\deff0\\nouicompat\\deflang2057{\\fonttbl{\\f0\\fnil Segoe UI;}}\r\n{\\colortbl ;\\red255\\green255\\blue255;}\r\n{\\*\\generator Riched20 3.2.0000}\\viewkind4\\uc1 \r\n\\pard\\tx720\\cf1\\f0\\fs21 The tunnels beneath the city hadn't appeared on any official map since the Interregnum. Mira had memorised them anyway.\\par\r\n}\r\n\u0000",
      "notes": "This chapter carries a lot of world-building weight — trim the history exposition in the second section. The Mira/Sable first meeting should feel accidental and tense, not convenient.",
